WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.090
- My first guest,

00:00:01.090 --> 00:00:02.470
he's someone who will always hold

00:00:02.470 --> 00:00:04.290
a very special place in my heart

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:06.810
because he was the first
person to interview me on TV

00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:08.390
after I won American Idol

00:00:08.390 --> 00:00:11.510
and he's also my favorite
host of all time.

00:00:11.510 --> 00:00:12.470
Take a look.

00:00:12.470 --> 00:00:14.210
- I mean, did you think you would win?

00:00:14.210 --> 00:00:15.050
Were you that confident?

00:00:15.050 --> 00:00:16.676
You can be modest but
you know what I'm saying.

00:00:16.676 --> 00:00:19.500
I'm not sure when you
enter these contests,

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:20.837
do you have in the back of your mind,

00:00:20.837 --> 00:00:21.670
"I can win this?"

00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:24.020
Do you just try to go week to week?

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:24.990
- Very day by day.

00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:26.330
I don't like to think too far ahead

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:27.710
or I'll start to stress myself out

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:31.360
but nobody coming into this
thought this show, for one,

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:33.190
I didn't think it was gonna be that huge.

00:00:33.190 --> 00:00:34.023
Then nobody thought,

00:00:34.023 --> 00:00:34.900
"You're gonna be the winner."

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:36.353
One out of 10,000?

00:00:36.353 --> 00:00:37.692
What are the odds?

00:00:37.692 --> 00:00:39.894
One out of 10,000.

00:00:39.894 --> 00:00:41.557
There you go.

00:00:41.557 --> 00:00:42.525
(crowd cheering)

00:00:42.525 --> 00:00:45.434
Please welcome the legendary Jay Leno!

00:00:45.434 --> 00:00:47.379
(crowd cheering)

00:00:47.379 --> 00:00:50.212
(hard rock music)

00:01:00.142 --> 00:01:02.059
- Thank you, thank you!

00:01:04.076 --> 00:01:05.716
- I'm so excited!

00:01:05.716 --> 00:01:08.026
- You know, thank you, thank you.

00:01:08.026 --> 00:01:09.710
Thank you very much.

00:01:09.710 --> 00:01:10.543
- I'm so excited!

00:01:10.543 --> 00:01:11.376
- I've always thought about how you said

00:01:11.376 --> 00:01:13.930
the odds of winning are one
in 10,000, what are the odds?

00:01:13.930 --> 00:01:15.920
And I said, well the
odds are one in 10,000!

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:18.390
It's a very simple question!

00:01:18.390 --> 00:01:20.253
- I at least caught myself

00:01:20.253 --> 00:01:21.086
'cause I was like,

00:01:21.086 --> 00:01:21.919
"What a dummy."

00:01:21.919 --> 00:01:22.752
- What are the odds of that?

00:01:22.752 --> 00:01:23.870
Well, they're one in 10,000!

00:01:23.870 --> 00:01:24.703
- But wait,

00:01:24.703 --> 00:01:26.210
do you hate watching
interviews of yourself

00:01:26.210 --> 00:01:27.043
when you're younger?

00:01:27.043 --> 00:01:27.980
I don't even do it.

00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:28.974
- I don't really watch,

00:01:28.974 --> 00:01:31.463
it's like Narcissus staring
at my own reflection.

00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:35.820
Once in a while something
comes up I wanna see

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:36.777
an old star or something,

00:01:36.777 --> 00:01:37.670
"Oh god, look at them."

00:01:37.670 --> 00:01:38.820
I'm not really looking at myself.

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:39.653
Not too much.

00:01:39.653 --> 00:01:41.190
- Oh, well that's because you're awesome.

00:01:41.190 --> 00:01:42.900
That was crazy, that was 17 years ago.

00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:44.037
- Just the fact that you said on TV,

00:01:44.037 --> 00:01:44.950
"I'm your first,"

00:01:44.950 --> 00:01:46.270
I thought that was surprising.

00:01:46.270 --> 00:01:50.437
(Kelly and crowd laugh and cheer)

00:01:52.757 --> 00:01:54.123
- It was so great.

00:01:55.240 --> 00:01:57.470
All right, well we actually dug up,

00:01:57.470 --> 00:01:59.770
because I love you so much, I do,

00:01:59.770 --> 00:02:01.893
a weird stalker love, but anyway,

00:02:02.830 --> 00:02:05.420
I found a picture from the first day,

00:02:05.420 --> 00:02:07.330
since this is the first season for me,

00:02:07.330 --> 00:02:09.570
I found a picture of you
hosting for the first time.

00:02:09.570 --> 00:02:10.403
Here we go.

00:02:10.403 --> 00:02:11.406
Look at you!

00:02:11.406 --> 00:02:13.989
(crowd cheers)

00:02:15.589 --> 00:02:16.422
My gosh!

00:02:17.672 --> 00:02:19.057
So handsome in your suit!

00:02:19.057 --> 00:02:20.638
- Yes, yes, so handsome.

00:02:20.638 --> 00:02:21.970
- You are handsome!

00:02:21.970 --> 00:02:22.803
- Well that's very kind.

00:02:22.803 --> 00:02:23.636
- You're my first.

00:02:23.636 --> 00:02:24.570
I wouldn't have given it
up if it wasn't handsome.

00:02:24.570 --> 00:02:25.509
- That's right, I was your first.

00:02:25.509 --> 00:02:27.610
(Kelly and crowd laugh)

00:02:27.610 --> 00:02:29.367
- Anybody tuning in right now would go,

00:02:29.367 --> 00:02:31.570
"Whoa, I didn't know that!

00:02:31.570 --> 00:02:33.329
That's how she got on the show!"

00:02:33.329 --> 00:02:34.645
- Yeah!

00:02:34.645 --> 00:02:35.478
(Kelly and crowd laugh)

00:02:35.478 --> 00:02:37.279
Well when you're good, you're good.

00:02:37.279 --> 00:02:38.199
- That's right.

00:02:38.199 --> 00:02:41.220
- No, I loved going on your show.

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:43.200
I thought you were just
so much fun and so kind

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:44.940
and you were just my favorite host.

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:46.180
I know I say that and it sounds cliche

00:02:46.180 --> 00:02:47.850
'cause you're on my show
but you were always so kind

00:02:47.850 --> 00:02:50.350
and you came to everybody's dressing room.

00:02:50.350 --> 00:02:51.780
That's my favorite thing about you.

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:55.030
You really invested in people
and it mattered and you cared.

00:02:55.030 --> 00:02:56.070
I thought that was really cool.

00:02:56.070 --> 00:02:56.903
- Oh, well thanks.

00:02:56.903 --> 00:02:58.880
I always like to talk to people.

00:02:58.880 --> 00:02:59.772
(crowd claps)

00:02:59.772 --> 00:03:03.130
You gave me a bottle of
wine, thank you very much.

00:03:03.130 --> 00:03:04.331
- I love wine.

00:03:04.331 --> 00:03:06.610
- My mom likes... I'm not a big wine.

00:03:06.610 --> 00:03:07.513
My mom,

00:03:08.870 --> 00:03:11.900
actually this kind of ties
in with daytime talk shows

00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:14.030
'cause my mom had a ritual.

00:03:14.030 --> 00:03:16.240
She would watch her story

00:03:16.240 --> 00:03:18.960
and then she would watch the Oprah.

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:20.200
Not Oprah.

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:21.763
The Oprah.

00:03:22.613 --> 00:03:23.446
- Kind of fits.

00:03:23.446 --> 00:03:26.908
- The older my mother got, the more wine.

00:03:26.908 --> 00:03:28.150
(Kelly laughs)

00:03:28.150 --> 00:03:29.440
So one day I go in the den

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:32.679
and I see the bottle's only
got about this much left

00:03:32.679 --> 00:03:35.850
and she's got this glassy look.

00:03:35.850 --> 00:03:38.667
My mother was from Scotland and she goes,

00:03:38.667 --> 00:03:40.290
"Jamie!

00:03:40.290 --> 00:03:41.750
Jamie, I got a question."

00:03:41.750 --> 00:03:42.847
"What is it, Mom?"

00:03:43.837 --> 00:03:45.267
"I'm watching the Oprah."

00:03:46.570 --> 00:03:47.547
She says,

00:03:47.547 --> 00:03:50.460
"And the lesbian people,

00:03:50.460 --> 00:03:52.460
I don't understand what it is they do

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:53.397
when they get together."

00:03:53.397 --> 00:03:55.873
"You know, Mom, this is a
little out of my wheelhouse.

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:58.426
Why don't you get Daddy in here.

00:03:58.426 --> 00:04:02.590
Not being a lesbian, I really
can't answer this question."

00:04:02.590 --> 00:04:03.990
It's one of those uncomfortable...

00:04:03.990 --> 00:04:05.577
My mother, she's got the wine, she goes,

00:04:05.577 --> 00:04:06.997
"I don't understand what they do."

00:04:06.997 --> 00:04:08.683
"I don't know what they do, Mom!"

